  $ p^x \( lambda - epsilon.alt_k + epsilon.alt_e \) & mapsto p^x \( lambda' - epsilon.alt_k \) \,\
p^x \( lambda - epsilon.alt_k - epsilon.alt_e \) & mapsto p^x \( lambda' - epsilon.alt_k \) . $
  Here $lambda'$ is the restricted highest weight; extend a positive-chamber cocharacter by zero in the last coordinate to verify that it is highest. The two ambient weight spaces are independent, so this restricted weight has multiplicity at least two. We show that an irreducible module of highest weight $p^x lambda'$ has multiplicity at most one there.
